,"source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# wall_stone\n\nStone wall: a straight segment one column (16 u) long along X, outer face toward -Z. End caps at both ends meet the next segment's cap to form a joint post. Stone: grey blocks, 3.6 m (128 u), one merlon, a walkway on top.\n\n- Footprint: 1 x 1 columns (16 x 16 units, 0.45 x 0.45 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -8..8, y 0..128, z -10..10 units.\n- Texture: 64 x 256, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 6, construction_0 16, construction_33 26, construction_66 28, ruined 8 (0 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 16 x 128 x 16 centred at x 0, z 0\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `wall_stone_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `wall_stone_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_wall_stone` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_wall_walk` at (0, 119, 2)\n"}